{"id": "tea:yuktisastika:35", "source": "src:yuktisastika", "location": {"ref": "35"}, "paraphrase": "When the Victors have said that nirvāṇa alone is true, what wise person would think that the rest is not false?", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "apophatic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:two-truths", "cpt:nirvana-in-madhyamaka"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yuktisastika:46-48", "source": "src:yuktisastika", "location": {"ref": "46-48"}, "paraphrase": "When things are accepted as real, fierce attachment and aversion and the grip of evil views arise, and disputes spring from them; that acceptance is the cause of all views, and without it afflictions do not arise; when it is fully understood, views and afflictions are exhausted — and it is understood by seeing dependent origination.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "consciousness-mind"], "obstacles": ["obs:svabhava-graha"], "terms": ["trm:drsti"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yuktisastika:5-6", "source": "src:yuktisastika", "location": {"ref": "5-6"}, "paraphrase": "Those who do not see reality conceive saṃsāra and nirvāṇa; those who see reality conceive neither. Existence and nirvāṇa are not two: the full understanding of existence is called nirvāṇa.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:samsara-nirvana-nondifference"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:yuktisastika:50", "source": "src:yuktisastika", "location": {"ref": "50"}, "paraphrase": "The great-souled have no thesis and no dispute; how could there be an opposing thesis for those who have no thesis?", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:no-thesis"], "disputes": ["dsp:debate-without-thesis"], "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U40-madhyamaka"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "teachers": ["tch:nagarjuna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U40-madhyamaka"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
